{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Deep Neural Network.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Deep Neural Network.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"deep neural network deep neural network","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Deep Neural Network.md","fileName":"Deep Neural Network.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Deep Neural Network","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 16:28\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Artificial Neural Network Structure]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Artificial Neural Network Structure","Artificial Neural Network","Backpropagation","Hidden Layer","Neural Depth Counting","Vanishing Gradient Problem","aiassistants.epub","algorithms.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Deep Neural Network.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Deep Neural Network.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"deep neural network deep neural network","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Deep Neural Network.md","fileName":"Deep Neural Network.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Deep Neural Network","heading":"Deep Neural Network","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A deep neural network is an [[Artificial Neural Network]] with multiple learned layers between input and output. Successive layers can transform raw features into progressively more useful internal representations.\n\nDepth lets a system learn complex mappings used in speech and language, but it also increases demands for data, computation, and careful optimization through [[Backpropagation]].\n\nEach [[Hidden Layer]] encodes a transformation of the representation produced before it. Successive layers can therefore build a hierarchy of concepts: an image network might progress from local edges to parts and then complete objects. This increasing level of abstraction is the sense in which the network and its learning are described as deep.\n\nKelleher counts [[Neural Depth Counting|depth]] by learned transformations: the hidden layers plus the output layer, or the number of weight matrices crossed. The input layer merely presents values. Additional depth increases representational flexibility, but it can also aggravate the [[Vanishing Gradient Problem]] unless the architecture and training setup support useful backward signals.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Artificial Neural Network Structure","Artificial Neural Network","Backpropagation","Hidden Layer","Neural Depth Counting","Vanishing Gradient Problem","aiassistants.epub","algorithms.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Deep Neural Network.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Deep Neural Network.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"deep neural network deep neural network","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Deep Neural Network.md","fileName":"Deep Neural Network.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Deep Neural Network","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[aiassistants.epub]]\n\n[[algorithms.epub]]\n\n[[deeplearning_mit.epub]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Artificial Neural Network Structure","Artificial Neural Network","Backpropagation","Hidden Layer","Neural Depth Counting","Vanishing Gradient Problem","aiassistants.epub","algorithms.epub","deeplearning_mit.epub"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}